// a predicate and its negation; "exhaustive b/c" after the cases, then "so P"
let n be an integer with n >= 2. wts n has a prime divisor
case n is prime. then n is a prime divisor of n.
case n is not prime. then n = ab for some integers a, b with 1 < a < n and 1 < b < n, and by induction a has a prime divisor p, which also divides n.
exhaustive b/c every integer is either prime or not, so n has a prime divisor
qed
